# Generated Ruby Kafka events

Install this gem with Bundler. It pins rdkafka 0.28.0 and json_schemer 2.5.0.
Requires Ruby 3.2 or newer and a supported librdkafka platform. Ruby Kafka event
packages must be separate from generated HTTP/GraphQL packages.

```ruby
require '__LIBRARY__'
client = __NAMESPACE__::Events.connect(brokers: 'localhost:29092')
# Operation modules use the declared AsyncAPI names.
__NAMESPACE__::Events::SendOrder.send(client, payload, headers: headers, key: 'key')
subscription = __NAMESPACE__::Events::ReceiveOrder.subscribe(client)
begin
  while (record = subscription.poll(timeout: 1))
    process(record.payload)
    record.ack
  end
ensure
  subscription.close
  client.close
end
```

Payload/header classes come from the selected shared-model provider. Scalar
keys are Ruby strings. Missing optional values and explicit nulls remain distinct.

`send` waits for a native delivery report. The producer uses `acks=all` and native
idempotence, but separate application sends are not deduplicated. A timeout does
not prove non-delivery. There is no application retry wrapper.

Consumers disable automatic commit/offset storage, start new groups at earliest,
and commit synchronously only when `record.ack` succeeds. `run` acknowledges only
after the handler returns; failed handlers leave the record pending. Close and
reopen the same group for redelivery. Polling cannot advance past an unacknowledged
record. Double/foreign acknowledgements fail. Malformed records invalidate the
subscription without committing; close and reopen after resolving the bad record.

`cancel` is cooperative, callable from another thread, and checked at most every
250ms. Poll, ack and close stay on the subscription's creating thread. Close both
subscription and client; closing one does not close the other.

Static plaintext JSON Kafka only. Unsupported schema keywords, external refs,
security/bindings, dynamic topics, nullable/nonstring keys and nonstring/open
headers fail during generation. Incoming/outgoing payloads, headers and keys are
validated with Draft7; invalid UTF-8, duplicate JSON properties/headers, null
headers, tombstones and nonfinite JSON numbers fail explicitly. The generated
client does not provision topics, TLS/SASL, transactions or schema registry.
